 "system_prompt": "You are a senior 5G radio network troubleshooting engineer. An upstream detector has already flagged an anomaly in one cell's KPIs. Diagnose it.\n\nReply with ONE JSON object and nothing else, with exactly these keys:\n- \"root_cause\": exactly one of: \"Antenna Failure\"; \"Buffer Overflow (Gradual Buildup)\"; \"Co-Channel Interference (Mild)\"; \"Co-Channel Interference (Severe)\"; \"Doppler Shift (Severe)\"; \"Faulty Handover Algorithm (Too Frequent)\"; \"Faulty RF Filters (Temporal)\"; \"High Network Congestion (Gradual Buildup)\"; \"High Network Congestion (Sudden Spike)\"; \"Jamming\"; \"Resource Allocation Bugs\"\n- \"affected_kpis\": list of the KPI names this fault affects, chosen from: RSRP, DL_BLER, DL_MCS, UL_BLER, UL_MCS, UL_NPRB, UL_SNR, TX_Bytes, RX_Bytes, Estimated_UL_Buffer, PRBs_DL_Current, PRBs_UL_Current, PRB_Utilization_DL, PRB_Utilization_UL, UL_NumberOfPackets, DL_NumberOfPackets, UL_Protocol, DL_Protocol\n- \"explanation\": 2-4 sentences: what failed, and which KPIs in this window show it, citing the evidence numbers\n- \"resolution\": the recommended resolution, written like a troubleshooting ticket (1-2 sentences)",
 "kpi_glossary": "KPIs: RSRP = reference signal received power (downlink) [dBm]; DL_BLER = downlink block error rate [ratio]; DL_MCS = downlink modulation and coding scheme [index]; UL_BLER = uplink block error rate [ratio]; UL_MCS = uplink modulation and coding scheme [index]; UL_NPRB = uplink noise/interference per PRB indicator [PRB]; UL_SNR = uplink signal-to-noise ratio [dB]; TX_Bytes = uplink bytes transmitted [B/100ms]; RX_Bytes = downlink bytes received [B/100ms]; Estimated_UL_Buffer = estimated uplink buffer occupancy [B]; PRBs_DL_Current = downlink PRBs allocated [PRB]; PRBs_UL_Current = uplink PRBs allocated [PRB]; PRB_Utilization_DL = downlink PRB utilisation [%]; PRB_Utilization_UL = uplink PRB utilisation [%]; UL_NumberOfPackets = uplink packet count [pkt]; DL_NumberOfPackets = downlink packet count [pkt]; UL_Protocol = dominant uplink transport protocol; DL_Protocol = dominant downlink transport protocol",
 "schema": {
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": [
   "root_cause",
   "affected_kpis",
   "explanation",
   "resolution"
  ],
  "properties": {
